  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Lead Capture**\n\nI\'m focusing on integrating a minimalist newsletter signup form into the footer. The goal is to capture lead data using a promise of \"B2B Automation Insights.\" The design should align with the established \'Editorial Aesthetic\' theme. I\'m currently examining `Footer.tsx` for implementation.\n\n\n**Refining Footer Structure**\n\nI\'m considering how best to integrate the lead capture into the existing footer layout. Initially, I\'m thinking of adding a new row above the existing four columns. Alternatively, modifying one of the existing columns to incorporate the signup form is also being explored. The current grid structure offers several opportunities for this addition. Perhaps a `md:grid-cols-5` approach is worth considering too.\n\n\n**Revising Footer Grid**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into adjusting the footer\'s grid system. My focus shifted to a 12-column grid to allow for a dedicated newsletter signup area. I\'ve re-examined the current `Footer.tsx` code, aiming for a structure where branding takes up 4 columns, product and resources 2 each, and the newsletter form also gets 4, with \"Rechtliches\" relegated to a bottom bar. The current design uses a 4 column grid; changing it will be the focal point of today.\n\n\n**Implementing Newsletter Signup**\n\nI\'ve crafted the newsletter signup form, complete with an email input and \"Abonnieren\" button. I\'ve used a minimalist, inline-border design, and the text uses German. It\'s designed to align with the overall minimalist design. The content is positioned within a flex container, and the email input is required. I\'ve designed it to be responsive, and incorporated appropriate styling.\n\n\n**Finalizing Footer Layout**\n\nI\'ve added the new bottom bar to the footer, which has refactored the design to an editorial aesthetic with legals and socials. The current state is looking much better. I\'m now looking at the code in `/src/components/Footer.tsx`, and making final layout tweaks.\n\n\n**Reviewing Branding Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating branding elements into the footer\'s bottom bar. My thoughts are centering on aligning the LeadPilot branding. I\'m focusing on the font and overall editorial aesthetic, and am thinking about how to adjust the layout to create the intended design. The current code in `/src/components/Footer.tsx` is my main focus.\n\n\n**Adding Product & Resources**\n\nI\'m now integrating \"Products\" and \"Resources\" links into the footer. I\'ve added these sections to `Footer.tsx` using a structure similar to the existing columns, focusing on the same styling for consistency. I am ensuring alignment and proper spacing, with each entry using the same text styles and hover effects.\n\n\n**Integrating Legal Links**\n\nI\'ve added the \"Rechtliches\" section to the bottom bar of the footer, incorporating links for Impressum, Datenschutz, and AGB. I\'ve designed them with an uppercase, tracking-widest font, consistent with the aesthetic, and the hover state mirrors other links. I\'ve integrated a link to LinkedIn as well, with the same minimalist styling. All of these links are in German.\n\n\n**Adjusting Footer Grid**\n\nI\'m now revising the footer grid layout for better structure, focusing on a 12-column grid. The goal is a layout with columns of 4, 2, 2, and 4 to properly allocate space for branding, product/resources, and the newsletter signup. I\'m focusing on the code in `Footer.tsx` to accommodate the modifications.\n\n\n**Refining Branding & Copy**\n\nI\'m now refining the branding section in `Footer.tsx`. The LeadPilot branding is receiving its final tweaks, and I\'m ensuring the copy is concise, clear, and impactful. The goal is to convey the value proposition succinctly. The current text uses \"Das KI-gest\303\274tzte Sales-CRM, das daf\303\274r sorgt, dass kein Lead im B2B-Mittelstand mehr vergessen wird.\"\n\n\n**Evaluating Resource Placement**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the placement of resources within the footer, specifically focusing on the structure and content of the \"Ressourcen\" section. I\'m considering whether the current organization\342\200\224Blog, Webinars, Help Center, and Customer Cases\342\200\224is optimal. I\'m focusing on consistency in styling and alignment with the editorial aesthetic. I\'m also ensuring the links are easily accessible and user-friendly.\n\n\n**Refining Form Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the newsletter signup form\'s functionality. I\'m focusing on the submission process, error handling, and success messaging. I am thinking about crafting an input with `type=\"email\"` and a placeholder, and a button. The goal is a user-friendly and effective signup process. I\'m working with the code in the footer.\n\n\n**Finalizing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on finalizing error handling for the newsletter form. I\'m focusing on ensuring clear and concise messages, and refining both input validation and submission error responses. I\'m aiming for a seamless user experience, with immediate feedback in case of errors. I\'m currently working with the `Footer.tsx` code.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 28
      nanos: 538901838
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
