  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Modal Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the modal\'s behavior. The goal is clear: clicking a data point in any of the specified charts \342\200\223 Funnel Bar, Forecast Line/Area/Month, or stage pills \342\200\223 triggers a modal. This overlay will then present a list of lead sources tied to that specific data point. I\'m also now planning on making a dedicated state for it.\n\n\n**Implementing Click Events**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating click events into the charts. I\'m adding `onClick` handlers to both `BarChart` and `ComposedChart` components, along with `Area` and `Line` components within the `ComposedChart`. These handlers will call helper functions: `openLeadSourcesForStage` and `openLeadSourcesForMonth`, which will handle how to properly open modal. I\'m also ensuring the cursor changes on hover for better user experience. Additionally, the explicit click events are being added to the tooltips to facilitate interaction.\n\n\n**Adding CTA for Lead Sources**\n\nI\'m now integrating a clickable CTA button to display lead sources. This includes adding the button to the stage summary sidebar and transition pills. I\'m focusing on making it clear and user-friendly, using an informative label like \"Lead-Quellen aufschl\303\274sseln\". Next, I\'ll focus on generating realistic lead source data, ensuring each stage and month has detailed contributions. Finally, I\'ll outline the structure of lead sources for stages, giving an example to clarify the contribution of sources.\n\n\n**Detailing Lead Source Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the structure for lead sources, providing specific examples for stages. For example, for \"Qualified & Initial Contact,\" I\'ve outlined the contributions of sources like AI speed calls and personalized email sequences, including lead counts, revenue volume, and percentage contribution. The format is consistent across the stages, ensuring clarity and detailed insight into each source\'s performance. The same is done for `demo` leads.\n\n\n**Illustrating Source Contributions**\n\nI\'m now detailing lead source contributions across different stages, using examples. For the \'proposal\' stage, I\'ve outlined lead counts, revenue volume, and percentage contribution for sources like SaaS Enterprise licenses and custom AI integrations. Similarly, for \'won\' stage, I\'m providing specific data on deals from sources like enterprise annual contracts and multi-year agreements. I\'m also preparing example data for forecast months, showing sources like LinkedIn Ads and website traffic and their corresponding revenue.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 966562351
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
